  "base_commit": "3bae1e9773d6b86e4feabd18cb9070d3416c3807",
  "pr_number": 5785,
  "issue_number": 5784,
  "issue_title": "Ill-Gotten Gains: non-targeted \"return up to N cards from graveyard\" silently drops its count, bouncing the entire graveyard",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n**Confirmed silent misparse** (verified against `data/card-data.json` and cross-checked with the live parser output on `main`). Not `Unimplemented` \u2014 the clause parses as a *valid*-looking `Effect::Bounce`, but the defining quantity is gone.\n\n## Card (verified against Scryfall)\n> Exile Ill-Gotten Gains. Each player discards their hand, then returns up to three cards from their graveyard to their hand.\n\n## Actual parse (current `main`)\nThe final clause lowers to:\n```\nBounce { target: Typed<Card, Owned:ScopedPlayer, InZone:Graveyard>, destination: None, selection: AtResolution }\n```\nwith **no `multi_target` at all**. There is nothing anywhere in the `AbilityDefinition` chain recording \"three.\" At resolution, the `EffectZoneChoice` picker has no bound to enforce, so each player would return their **entire graveyard** to hand instead of up to three cards \u2014 the exact opposite of a \"restraint\" ability card text, and a significant rules violation (CR 601.2c \"up to N\" semantics never applied).\n\n## Root cause\n`TargetedImperativeAst::Return` (the non-targeted, at-resolution bounce variant \u2014 used whenever Oracle text omits the word \"target\", e.g. \"return a card from your graveyard to your hand\") has no count-carrying field at all, unlike its sibling `Tap`/`Untap`/`Fight`, which already carry `multi_target: Option<MultiTargetSpec>` for exactly this \"up to N\" shape.\n\nSeparately, the \"return \" clause dispatchers (`parse_targeted_action_ast` in `oracle_effect/imperative.rs` and `try_parse_verb_and_target` in `oracle_effect/mod.rs`) never call the existing `strip_any_number_quantifier` building block for this shape \u2014 even though `\"return\"` is already listed in its `MULTI_TARGET_VERBS` table and the helper is proven correct for the sibling `Tap`/`Untap` \"up to N target creatures\" pattern. Left unstripped, the leading \"up to three \" is silently absorbed as unrecognized filler by the downstream destination/target parser.\n\nThe *targeted* sibling shape (\"return up to two **target** cards from your graveyard to your hand\" \u2014 Seeds of Renewal, Restock) already works correctly today, via a completely different code path (`strip_optional_target_prefix`, gated on the literal word \"target\"). Only the non-targeted, \"target\"-keyword-less shape is affected.\n\n## Runtime is unaffected\n`Effect::Bounce`'s at-resolution `EffectZoneChoice` picker already correctly resolves a bounded `ability.multi_target` \u2014 this is exercised today by `game::effects::bounce::non_targeted_optional_bounce_still_prompts_at_resolution` and `targeted_up_to_two_graveyard_bounce_moves_chosen_creature` (Wrenn and Six / Macabre Waltz). This is a pure parser-side gap; no game-logic change is required.\n\n## Scope \u2014 one confirmed card, a real architectural gap\nIll-Gotten Gains is the only card in the current pool matching this *exact* non-targeted numeric shape (`grep`'d against MTGJSON `AtomicCards.json` for `returns? (up to \\w+|that many) cards? from (your|their) \\w+ to (your|their) \\w+` with no `target` keyword). The sibling card `Bound // Determined` (\"Return up to X cards from your graveyard to your hand, where X is the number of colors that creature was\") uses the same non-targeted shape but is additionally broken by a separate, pre-existing bug in \"where X is `<description>`\" CDA-quantity binding (the resolved `Variable` ends up holding the literal description string instead of a resolved quantity) \u2014 **out of scope here**, filed as a distinct concern.\n\n### Related, NOT fixed here (follow-up)\nThe same *class* of defect (a bounded \"up to N\" quantifier dropped on a non-targeted, at-resolution zone-transfer effect) also reproduces on **Stream of Thought** (\"You shuffle up to four cards from your graveyard into your library\") via the entirely separate `shuffle ... into` recognizer (`parse_shuffle_ast` in `oracle_effect/imperative.rs`). Different AST family (`ShuffleImperativeAst`, not `TargetedImperativeAst::Return`), so it needs its own fix \u2014 flagged here as an untriaged sibling lead, not addressed by the PR accompanying this issue.\n\n## Fix shape\n- Add `multi_target: Option<MultiTargetSpec>` to `TargetedImperativeAst::Return`, mirroring the existing `Tap`/`Untap`/`Fight` pattern.\n- Wire the existing `strip_any_number_quantifier` building block into both \"return \" dispatchers, restricted to the genuinely bounded (`max: Some(_)`) result so the unrelated unbounded \"any number of\" shape (Grave Sifter class, its own pre-existing `return_up_to`/`ReturnToZone.up_to` mechanism) is left untouched.\n- Thread the captured spec onto the clause in the shared `lower_imperative_family_ast` interception point, reusing the already-tested `EffectZoneChoice` runtime seam \u2014 no game-logic changes.\n\nCR references: CR 601.2c (\"up to N\" targeting/selection cardinality), CR 115.1d (variable target/object counts), CR 400.6/CR 400.7 (zone-change origin/destination).",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-14T12:32:57.000Z",
